#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial simulates the Trotterized time evolution of the tilted-field "
"Ising model with the LTM AI-QEM function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Originally conceptualized to understand ferromagnetism and quantum phase "
"transitions in magnetic materials, the Ising model [[1]](#references) has "
"become a cornerstone of modern many-body physics. At its fundamental level, "
"the model describes a lattice of interacting spins, where each spin can "
"occupy one of two states and interacts with its nearest neighbors. The real-"
"time dynamics of two-dimensional Ising systems become increasingly difficult"
" to simulate classically as the system size and evolution time increase, "
"which makes them an important testbed for quantum simulation. Moreover, "
"because the Hamiltonian is composed of local single-qubit fields and "
"nearest-neighbor two-qubit interactions, its time evolution can be naturally"
" represented with sequences of single- and two-qubit quantum gates. These "
"properties make the model a useful benchmark for studying quantum dynamics "
"on present-day hardware and for evaluating the effectiveness of quantum "
"error mitigation methods.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial covers the following steps:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Describe the tilted-field Ising model and its Trotterized time evolution "
"mathematically.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Define the backend and the qubits on which to simulate the Hamiltonian, and "
"visualize them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Define the tilted-field Ising Hamiltonian with the Qiskit `SparsePauliOp` "
"class.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Construct the quantum circuits for the evolution of the Hamiltonian with the"
" Qiskit `evolved_operator_ansatz` function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Define the observable that corresponds to the average magnetization, again "
"with the `SparsePauliOp` class.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute the evolution of the average magnetization for an increasing number "
"of Trotter steps with the LTM AI-QEM function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Apply the zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) method to the raw QPU results, to "
"compare against the mitigation performed by the LTM AI-QEM function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"List the values of the average magnetization computed with the sparse Pauli "
"dynamics (SPD) algorithm, which serve as the ideal values.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Visualize all of the results to compare the average magnetization mitigated "
"by LTM AI-QEM with the unmitigated results, the results mitigated by ZNE, "
"and the results from the classical SPD algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""

